This product is designed to build on, and interoperate with, the following
open-source projects (not vendored here; installed as dependencies or used as
external oracles):

  * Newton physics engine — Apache-2.0 (NVIDIA / Google DeepMind / Disney
    Research; Linux Foundation). https://github.com/newton-physics/newton
    NOTE: lumen/newton/vbd_fork.py is a derivative of Newton's SolverVBD
    (newton/_src/solvers/vbd/solver_vbd.py, Apache-2.0), modified to inject the
    tube-intrinsic contact barrier into the per-color AVBD solve. Original
    copyright (c) 2025 The Newton Developers; modifications (c) 2026 Seldinger.
  * NVIDIA Warp — Apache-2.0. https://github.com/NVIDIA/warp
  * STARK / SymX — accurate-tier oracle (cross-validation only).
  * ppf-contact-solver — GPU accurate-tier baseline (cross-validation only).
  * DiffDRR — differentiable X-ray rendering (sensor layer).
  * TotalSegmentator — Apache-2.0 (University Hospital Basel). Optional; installed only
    when the user agrees during `lumen import`, from the pinned fork
    https://github.com/SeldingerMed/TotalSegmentator.
  * RSNA 2025 intracranial artery model and nnXNet — Apache-2.0 (Pengcheng Shi and
    co-authors). Optional; installed only when the user agrees during `lumen import`,
    from the pinned fork
    https://github.com/SeldingerMed/RSNA2025_Intracranial-Aneurysm-Detection.

This repository deliberately does NOT depend on or derive from CathSim
(CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0). Patient-derived geometry appears only in the open cases listed
below, each derived from a public, de-identified scan whose licence allows
redistribution; tools/check_firewall.py enforces both rules. Anatomy a user imports
from their own scan with `lumen import` is written to a folder the user chooses and
is never part of this repository.


Open cases shipped in lumen/cases/ (derived vessel geometry only; no images):

  * head-cta-aneurysm, head-neck-cta — derived from studies 006 and 002 of
    Blagosklonova E, Dolotova D, Polunina N, Grigorieva E, Pakhomov D, Krylov V, et al.,
    "Open dataset of annotated DICOM images of head CTA for intracranial aneurysm
    detection", Zenodo, doi:10.5281/zenodo.15697196. CC BY 4.0.
  * aorta-cta — derived from case D10 of Radl L, Jin Y, Pepe A, Li J, Gsaxner C, Zhao F,
    Egger J, "AVT: Multicenter aortic vessel tree CTA dataset collection with ground
    truth segmentation masks", Data in Brief 40:107801 (2022),
    doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.14806362. CC BY 4.0.
  * abdomen-cta — derived from scan s1405 of the TotalSegmentator dataset v2.0.1,
    Wasserthal J et al., "TotalSegmentator: robust segmentation of 104 anatomic
    structures in CT images", Radiology: Artificial Intelligence 5(5):e230024 (2023),
    doi:10.5281/zenodo.10047292. CC BY 4.0.
  * head-tof-mra — derived from sub-000 of Di Noto T et al., "Lausanne TOF-MRA Aneurysm
    Cohort", OpenNeuro ds003949 v1.0.1, doi:10.18112/openneuro.ds003949.v1.0.1. CC0.

Changes made: the arteries were segmented from the scan by `lumen import` (head: the
RSNA 2025 intracranial model; body: TotalSegmentator), converted to centre lines with
cross-sections, and the vessel surface was simplified. Each case's case.json repeats
its source, licence and citation.


Procedural anatomy pack policy:

  * `lumen.assets.anatomy_pack` contains only geometry generated by
    `lumen.assets.procedural`; it contains no patient-derived measurements or
    externally licensed anatomy.
  * Pack metadata is released under Apache-2.0 with
    `provenance="procedural"` and records the generator source.
  * The open cases in `lumen/cases/` are not procedural; they keep their sources'
    licences (above), not Apache-2.0.
  * A contributed anatomy case MUST ship reproducible generator parameters,
    provenance, and license metadata. Patient-derived or unclear-license assets
    belong outside this repository behind the private asset seam.
